cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the bundled PSGC dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "barangay: Offline Python package for the Philippine Standard Geographic Code (PSGC)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Balmeo"
    given-names: "Manuel"
type: software
version: "2026.4.13.4"
date-released: "2026-06-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bendlikeabamboo/barangay"
url: "https://bendlikeabamboo.github.io/barangay/"
abstract: >-
  barangay provides offline, in-process access to the Philippine Standard
  Geographic Code (PSGC): all 42,011 barangays, 1,488 municipalities, 146
  cities, 82 provinces, and 17 regions, with fuzzy search, address validation,
  hierarchy traversal, pandas export, and historical PSGC snapshots. Based on
  the official PSA PSGC masterlist.
keywords:
  - Philippines
  - PSGC
  - barangay
  - geocoding
  - fuzzy search
  - address validation
  - open data
